          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "zelwm68",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Crust"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "poetqvx",
      "content": "• Outermost layer of the Earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "27zjyzz",
      "content": "• Thickness varies from about 5 km (oceanic crust) to 70 km (continental crust)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gtuzkd0",
      "content": "• Mainly composed of oxygen, silicon, aluminium, iron and calcium."
    },
    {
      "id": "byyh6fa",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Types of Crust"
    },
    {
      "id": "32l8amt",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Thickness</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Composition</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Continental Crust</p>",
            "<p>30–70 km</p>",
            "<p>Granite rich in silica and alumina</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Oceanic Crust</p>",
            "<p>5–10 km</p>",
            "<p>Basalt rich in silica and magnesium</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
